I am off from work.
I walk out onto a large square.
There are many people in the city today.
A man walks up to me.
He has a large camera.
He is a tourist.
He smiles and says hi.
"Excuse me, do you speak English?" he asks.
"Yes, I speak English," I answer.
"Where is the museum?" the tourist asks.
I know the museum well.
It is not far away.
I point down the street.
"You walk straight ahead," I explain.
"Then you turn to the left."
"The museum is on the right side."
"Thank you very much for the help," the man says.
"You are welcome," I answer happily.
He walks down the street.
I walk on towards the bakery.
